  "notes": [
    "Episode onset is the first second whose trailing 60 s was >=90% below MAP 65 (build_dataset.hypotension_flags). So at the onset the patient has already been hypotensive for about a minute by construction, which gives a MAP-keyed alarm such as rule_map65 a structural head start.",
    "Event metrics use each variant's validation-tuned threshold for sensitivity >= 0.80, except the rule_map65* variants, whose as-designed threshold is 0 (MAP <= 65).",
    "Alarms are rising edges on the 30 s decision grid, so a sustained high score counts once.",
    "Mode `significance` resamples windows and is therefore anti-conservative; the case-level intervals here are the ones to quote.",
    "The label looks 300 s ahead, and the same span is the actionable alarm window of an episode (see the `pre` argument of event_metrics). Event metrics are therefore only comparable between runs that share --horizon."
  ]
}